  "interpretation": "In the TB-A01 editorial-fashion transfer context, explicit garment-construction geometry modestly improved visible garment-construction fidelity relative to the generic dress description. The construction condition scored 5.00 on garment_construction_fidelity versus 4.75 for the control, a variant-minus-control delta of +0.25. Semantic compliance, aesthetic quality, and technical-defect cleanliness were unchanged between conditions, and the overall mean improved by only +0.0625. The result therefore weakly supports the tested hypothesis in this context rather than establishing a broad rule that more garment-construction detail is always beneficial.",
